inted one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-master-dichotomy"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-master-dichotomy"],"id":"long.thm-master-dichotomy","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.60 (Nonmembership of one half and a finite fatal gap)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.60, p. 61, label thm:master-dichotomy","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*The value $1/2$ is not in $\\mathcal A$ if and only if there are an integer $d\\ge0$ and a finite set $u\\subseteq\\{1,\\ldots,d\\}$ such that\n$$\nX_u(2)+R_{d+1}<\\frac12<X_u(2)+w_{d+1}.\n$$\nOne implication is Lemma 6.37. For the other, follow the greedy prefixes: nonmembership forces a first failure of the tail inequality, hence one of these gaps. The endpoint equalities are excluded by Lemma 6.38.*\n\n*A finite prefix and strict gap provide a nonmembership witness. The tail inequality can be certified by rational truncation bounds as in Theorem 2.11. Membership, in contrast, asserts that no such witness exists; failure to find one in a finite search is not a proof. The reduction uses $w_n>R_n$, not compactness alone. The totient weights fail this hypothesis, as the example after Lemma 6.34 shows.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-master-dichotomy","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-master-dichotomy","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-master-dichotomy%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.half_mem_mersenneAchievementSet_iff_no_existsFatalHalfGap%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-master-dichotomy%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.half_mem_mersenneAchievementSet_iff_no_existsFatalHalfGap%22%2C%2